@startuml
' Scenario-time alignment over one bench cycle.
' Values from Scenario_Player/scenarios/default.yaml (cpm_rate_hz 10, duration_s 20, loop true),
' the Phase 1 run record (60 m start, 2.5 m/s closing), and R13 (gate_enter 30 m, gate_exit 35 m).
' Horizontal axis is bench scenario time t in seconds.

title One 20 s bench cycle — the 12.0 s lead-in is what absorbs start misalignment

concise "Bench scenario time t [s]" as T
concise "C reported distance (R2 object.distance)" as D
concise "B track state (own_sensor, R13)" as B
concise "C track state (v2x_relayed, R13)" as C
concise "R4 warning to IVI" as W

@0
T is "t = 0 — cycle start"
D is "60 m"
B is "detector warm-up"
C is not_tracked
W is silent

@1
T is {hidden}

@5
B is "tracked (B confirmed)"

@10
D is "35 m — gate_exit level"

@12
D is "30 m — gate_enter crossed"
C is tentative

@13
C is tracked
W is "warning emitted"

@20
T is "t = 0 — loop restarts"
D is "60 m"
C is not_tracked
W is silent

highlight 0 to 12 #LightGreen : lead-in — 12.0 s of slack for detector warm-up + B confirmation
highlight 12 to 20 #Gold : C in gate — 8.0 s of warning window per cycle

@enduml
